/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 49 0 R
/T (Res ipsa loquitur is a legal doctrine meaning "the thing speaks for itself." It allows a court to infer negligence based purely on the nature of an accident, even without direct proof of how it happened.)
/E (Res ipsa loquitur is a legal doctrine meaning "the thing speaks for itself." It allows a court to infer negligence based purely on the nature of an accident, even without direct proof of how it happened.)
/Pg 15 0 R
